HOW TO USE:

To run the program type "python chess.py" into the terminal.

Once the program begins to run you will be prompted for White's move type in "(source)-(destination)" both the source and destination should be formatted with the column letter first followed by the row number. There should be no spaces and it does not matter if the column letter is upper or lower case.

If the move is valid the program will display the updated board and prompt for the opposite color's move. If the move is invalid then the displayed board will be the same as the last one and will prompt for the current color's move again.

This will continue until 'q' is typed into the terminal which will end the current game or when one of the kings is captured. Whoever's king is still standing at the end of the game will be declared the winner.


