Bugs found:

- Allows pawns to move backwards to take pieces (Fixed)

- Allows pawns to move forward across an entire file and capture pieces on the same file (Fixed)

- Allows pawns to jump across the board and take a piece one file away meaning white can capture a the king immediatly with the D2 pawn (Fixed)

- Reports that the king is in check when it is not in check (Fixed)

- Returns that a Knight can move across any rank or file even though it should not (Fixed)

- Does not update the king to keep track of the current location meaning it always thinks it is on its starting position and does not allow it to move more than one place away (Fixed)

- Allowed players to take their own pieces (Fixed)

- Queens and rooks can jump over pieces when they are moving horizontally along the board, with no limit to the number of pieces jumped over. (Fixed)

- Black pieces (untested for pawns) can move backwards to a ninth row, and be redirected onto the first row and kill the white pieces. Does not work with a 10th or 11th row. (Fixed)